  << /ActualText (Essentially\054 what I do through my work and the work through the program at SCI\055Arc is a world building program\056 It\031s a technique that comes from cinema that basically rewires the traditional linear process of telling stories\056 So\054 traditionally a film would start with a script and that script would start to get names attached\054 get funding and then at that point it would go into development\054 bringing a production designer on board to flesh out the world of that film\056 You would then shoot\054 edit and post produce it to make the film\056\nWorld building puts the creation of the world before all of that\056 Rather than developing a script\054 a narrative or a set of characters you develop a world\056 You then inhabit that world with characters\054 a story\054 and just following those characters through their most logical interactions of the spaces and structures in the world around them \055 this is an architectural way of thinking about film\056\nOne of the big proponents of world building is Alex McDowell who was the production designer that worked on Stephen Spielberg\031s Minority Report\056 He came on board with a group of technologists and futurists well before there was a script for the film\056 They were tasked with imagining this future city and they developed the whole design for that city\056 They imagined where it would sit in America\054 the traffic infrastructure and the road network \055 even the nature of the screen in this future world\056 The gestural interface\054 for example\054 was developed as real tech with a group of designers and technologists from Silicon Valley\056 Out of that one film came over 100 patents for new technologies\056\nHow they developed the story from there was simply to put Tom Cruise\047s character into that world\056 They then started writing a script\056\050The vertical car chase was only something that could have emerged\0501\051 if you had designed the world in the first place\056 It required the vertical traffic network \055 with the mechanisms and concepts of that specific transportation infrastructure in place \055 only then could you have Tom Cruise\031s character crash out the window of his apartment and start hitching rides on cars driving on the sides of buildings\056\nThat\047s really what we do at SCI\055Arc\054 we design imaginary worlds that become the setting for stories and we use them as a way of looking back on our own world in new ways\054 and that is something that I think architects do really well\056)
     /K [ 28 ]
     /P 1215 0 R
     /Pg 1158 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

