1256 0 obj
  << /ActualText (What we\047re doing at the moment is looking at the themes of the post\055human\056 By that\0505\051  I don\047t mean cyborgs and replacing eyeballs with digital lenses\056 I mean thinking about the ways that a lot of our spaces and cities are being designed not for people any longer but for machines or at the very least machine vision\056\nWe are exploring new narratives that don\047t put the human at the centre of the story\056 Instead we look at the alternative subject positions that emerge when some of the dominant actors in this space are actually algorithms or the countless bestiary of machines\056\nWe did a film \030Where the City Can\031t See\031 which is told in part from the perspective of a driverless car\056 It\047s a film that is shot entirely through laser scanners\054 the technology that driverless cars use to see and scan the world\056 It is the first of our explorations into what it means for a story to be told from the perspective of an autonomous vehicle\056\nIn another film we produced \030In the Robot Skies\031\056 The drone was the active narrative engine of the film\056 What we did was program a series of GPS points from which the drone could make its own decisions about how to catalogue the characters and their reactions\056 The actors are just running through their scenes over and over again\056 The drone would follow them initially and start to make its own choices of what it wanted to focus on\056 )
     /K [ 49 ]
     /P 1257 0 R
     /Pg 1158 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

